isor role is geared toward supporting student success, providing both academic and career advising while maintaining high standards of professionalism and collaboration within their respective college. CBAS has an established Advising Center with high professional standards and a reputation for excellence. The best qualified candidate is student-centered, communicates clearly and effectively, is a team player, advocates for STEM, and is capable of working effectively with staff and faculty to serve the diverse needs of students.\n\nThe Advanced Academic Advisor builds upon the foundational role of the Academic Advisor, offering deeper expertise in academic planning, student engagement, and retention strategies. This position focuses on providing enhanced advising services to specialized student populations, including transfer students, at-risk students, and those in specific academic disciplines. The Advanced Advisor works closely with faculty and administrative staff to ensure that students meet academic goals and are on track for graduation. The role also includes involvement in professional development and special projects that contribute to the overall success of the advising center. Perform related tasks and special projects as assigned. Note: a flexible work schedule is required to accommodate student requests for advising after traditional work hours. Maintenance Supervisor - TN Miller Coliseum Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Facilities Services - Maintenance, Other Perform a variety of repair and preventative maintenance tasks including electrical, plumbing, HVAC, carpentry, metal fabrication, and masonry for the Tennessee Miller Coliseum. Operate HVAC system controls to ensure appropriate cooling or heating of indoor spaces. Arrange and oversee maintenance service from external contractors or other university departments. Train, schedule, and supervise part-time maintenance staff. Perform other tasks as assigned. Executive Assistant -  Jones College of Business Advising Center Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Business The Jones College of Business at Middle Tennessee State University invites applications for an Executive Assistant in the Undergraduate Advising Center. This position serves as a key member of the advising team and provides comprehensive administrative, operational, and student support services that contribute to student success, retention, and timely degree completion.\n\nThe Executive Assistant serves as the primary point of contact for students, prospective students, parents, faculty, staff, and campus partners interacting with the Undergraduate Advising Center. Responsibilities include coordinating advising appointments, managing high-volume student communications, assisting with registration and graduation processes, maintaining student records, supporting advising initiatives, processing employment documents in the hiring verification workflow, and helping students navigate university policies and procedures.\n\nThe position also supports the daily operations of the Advising Center through office management, event coordination, communication and outreach efforts, data reporting, purchasing, scheduling, and technology support. The Executive Assistant assists with planning and implementing orientation programs, recruitment activities, advising workshops, and other student success initiatives while maintaining confidentiality and ensuring compliance with university policies and FERPA regulations.\n\nThe successful candidate will possess excellent organizational, communication, customer service, and problem-solving skills; the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment; and experience using technology and information systems to support student services. This position plays an important role in fostering a welcoming, student-centered environment and advancing the mission of the Jones College Undergraduate Advising Center. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 21e75660 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administrative/Clerical Support College of Business Administrative/Clerical Support College of Business Employment Type Classified Classified Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) ee4ae0ca Last Name (required) fa78e0e4 Email (required) 875a2213 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagram Youtube Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
