      "title": "Specialist",
      "description": "Specialist - Tech Support\t - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Visit MTSU Why Choose MTSU Applicant Log In My Profile Kiosk mode Specialist - Tech Support 498689 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Admissions and Enrollment Information Technology Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Specialist - Tech Support Department Undergraduate Recruitment Salary $59,724 - $74,355; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function Reporting to the Associate Director of Communications and Technology, maintains the data integrity and operations of the Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system (Slate), supporting the data and system functionality needed for communications and recruitment activities across Undergraduate Admissions and other Enrollment Management departments. Provide training and technical support to admissions staff in accessing and using Slate for various recruitment activities, promoting efficient and effective use. Maintain data integrity through thorough data cleaning, validation, and quality control to ensure accuracy and reliability. Develop queries to meet university reporting needs across multiple data areas and criteria. Pull and distribute multiple reports each week to support recruitment, enrollment, and other university reporting needs, providing analysis and insights as needed. Participate in special projects and perform additional responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Undergraduate Recruitment and the Associate Director. Required Education Bachelor's degree in a technical field such as computer science, data science, or other related field. Required Related Experience Three years of related technical experience. Desirable Related Experience Experience working with relational databases, CRM systems, query development, and data reporting, Slate or a similar higher education is preferred. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: September 28, 2026 Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant - Military Science Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Basic & Applied Sciences, Other Serves as the Executive Assistant and secretary to the Chair of the Military Science Department at Middle Tennessee State University (MTSU), providing comprehensive administrative and clerical support to the department and Army ROTC program. Assists students with administrative and educational needs, performs routine secretarial and office management duties, maintains office supplies and records, and coordinates major ROTC events, including commissioning and awards ceremonies. Serves as secretary for the ROTC Alumni Chapter, prepares and processes correspondence in accordance with university policies and military standards, and ensures accurate, professional, and timely communication with students, faculty, staff, military personnel, alumni, and external organizations. Supports the overall day-to-day operations of the Military Science Department and Army ROTC program while maintaining a high level of professionalism, organization, confidentiality, and attention to detail. Executive Assistant - Philosophy and Religious Studies Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Liberal Arts Provide administrative support to the students, faculty, and chair for the department of Philosophy and Religious Studies and contribute to the successful operation of the department. Tasks might include: compose correspondence; maintain files and reports; monitor and maintain department expenses and reporting; initiate travel arrangements for conferences or special events; prepare adjunct faculty and department contracts; develop and maintain enrollments and course offerings; maintain key and equipment inventory; order office equipment and supplies; monitor tasks of student workers; schedule meetings, agendas, oversee website and any social media accounts, assist with internships, facilitate relationships with the Dean's office, etc. Perform other related tasks as assigned. Licensed Practical Nurse (LPN) Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Health Services Room patients and assist with physical examinations/procedures\nAdministering medications\nTake accurate patient history and update chart\nEKGs\nPFTs\nPerform limited laboratory procedures according to medical protocols\nMaintain and clean supplies and equipment for use by health personnel\nObtain vital signs, obtain samples and perform clinical tests © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagram Youtube Candidate Details We use cookies Some a