    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/psychology-clinical-tenure-track-faculty-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states-ad5af5c0-9e8d-446b-baf1-3731de5b4230": {
      "title": "Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty",
      "description": "Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Visit MTSU Why Choose MTSU Applicant Log In My Profile Kiosk mode Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty 498681 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Psychology and Human/Social/Protective Services Tenure-Track Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Psychology (Clinical), Tenure-Track Faculty Department Psychology University Expectation MTSU seeks candidates committed to innovative teaching, robust research/creative activity, and meaningful service. We also seek to attract culturally and academically diverse faculty who value working with diverse students. Salary The salary is commensurate with education and experience. Job Summary/Basic Function The Department of Psychology at Middle Tennessee State University invites applicants for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position (#120310) in clinical psychology at the rank of assistant or associate professor. The start date for the position is August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will join a department of dedicated faculty who support several popular undergraduate minors, two undergraduate majors, four master's-level graduate majors, and one graduate major at the specialist's level. Faculty in the clinical area also support the undergraduate mental health services minor, the undergraduate psychology major, and the clinical psychology master’s program. Located on the edge of the greater Nashville area, MTSU is an ideal setting for a wide range of research and service-related interests. Key Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses, including both area-specific topics (e.g., psychopathology, cross-cultural clinical practice, evidence-based treatment) and broader departmental needs (e.g., general psychology, personality, biopsychology). Mentor students in thesis and capstone projects. Develop and maintain an active research program. Participate in departmental, university, and community service activities. Required Education A terminal degree in clinical psychology or other health services psychology field from an APA-accredited training program that also included an APA-accredited internship is required by the appointment date. Other Desirables Applicants with the following will receive special consideration. Eligible for licensure in Tennessee as a psychologist with the health services provider designation. Demonstrated interest in clinical training at the master's level. Demonstrated potential for external funding in research, community engagement, or contracts. Documents Needed to Apply To successfully apply, applicants must include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of teaching philosophy, and statement of research or creative activities (as appropriate to the discipline) as separate attachments when submitting the application. Special Instruction to Applicants If you need help with the application, please contact Mitzi Dunkley, Faculty Recruitment Specialist, at (615) 898-5128. If you have position-specific questions, please contact James Loveless at James.Loveless@mtsu.edu. MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee, their spouse, and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email emp@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: 10/10/2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 7ddc990f Last Name (required) f1b70198 Email (required) 9b863dbc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Specialist - Tech Support Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Admissions and Enrollment, Information Technology Reporting to the Associate Director of Communications and Technology, maintains the data integrity and operations of the Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system (Slate), supporting the data and system functionality needed for communications and recruitment activities across Undergraduate Admissions and other Enrollment Management departments. Provide training and technical support to admissions staff in accessing and using Slate for various recruitment activities, promoting efficient and effective use. Maintain data integrity through thorough data cleaning, validation, and quality control to ensure accuracy and reliability. Develop queries to meet university reporting needs across multiple data areas and criteria. Pull and distribute multiple reports each week to support recruitment, enrollment, and other university reporting needs, providing analysis and insights as needed. Participate in special projects and perform additional responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Undergraduate Recruitment and the Associate Director. Executive Assistant - Military Science Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Basic & Applied Sciences, Other Serves as the Executive Assistant and secretary to the Chair of the Military Science Department at Middle Tennessee State University (MTSU), providing comprehensive administrative and clerical support to the department and Army ROTC program. Assists students with administrative and educational needs, performs routine secretarial and office management duties, maintains office supplies and records, and coordinates major ROTC events, including commissioning and awards ceremonies. Serves as secretary for the ROTC Alumni Chapter, prepares and processes correspondence in accordance with university policies and military standards, and ensures accurate, professional, and timely communication with students, faculty, staff, military personnel, alumni, and external organizations. Supports the overall day-to-day operations of the Military Science Department and Army ROTC program while maintaining a high level of professionalism, organization, confidentiality, and attention to detail. Executive Assistant - Philosophy and Religious Studies Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Administrative/Clerical Support, College of Liberal Arts Provide administrative support to the students, faculty, and chair for the department of Philosophy and Religious Studies and contribute to the successful operation of the department. Tasks might include: compose correspondence; maintain files and reports; monitor and maintain department expenses and reporting; initiate travel arrangements for conferences or special events; prepare adjunct faculty and department contracts; develop and maintain enrollments and course offerings; maintain key and equipment inventory; order office equipment and supplies; monitor tasks of student workers; schedule meetings, agendas, oversee website and any social media accounts, assist with internships, facilitate relationships with the Dean's office, etc. Perform other related tasks as assigned. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e7f38225 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Psychology and Human/Social/Protective Services Psychology and Human/Social/Protective Services Employment Type Tenure-Track Tenure-Track Locations Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States First Name (required) 407007bb Last Name (required) a9c48bf0 Email (required) 3ae636bf Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026 Middle Tennessee State University Cookie Preferences Nondiscrimination Policy Terms Follow Us: Facebook LinkedIn X Instagram Youtube Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
