    "https://careers.mtsu.edu/jobs/specialist-recruitment-murfreesboro-tennessee-tennessee-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist",
      "description": "Specialist - Recruitment - Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Visit MTSU Why Choose MTSU Applicant Log In My Profile Kiosk mode Specialist - Recruitment 498683 Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee, United States Admissions and Enrollment Student Affairs and Services Administrative Add to favorites View favorites Job Title Specialist - Recruitment Department Undergraduate Recruitment Salary $48,920 - $60,252; commensurate with experience Job Summary/Basic Function Reporting to the Director of Undergraduate Recruitment, the Specialist - Recruitment supports the recruitment and enrollment of prospective students through on-campus recruitment activities, student engagement, and event programming. The Specialist - Recruitment serves as a primary point of contact for prospective students and their families visiting Middle Tennessee State University and represents the University in a professional, welcoming, and knowledgeable manner. Essential duties include providing information to prospective students and families; assisting with on-campus recruitment events and campus tours; maintaining regular communication with prospective students; supporting recruitment initiatives and special projects; and collaborating with campus partners to provide a positive and seamless prospective student experience. Evening and weekend work is required to support recruitment events and activities. Required Education Bachelor's degree required. Required Related Experience One year of full-time experience in higher education. Required License/Registration/Certification Valid driver's license required. Desirable Related Experience One year of full-time experience in admissions, recruitment, enrollment management, student services, or a related field is preferred. Documents Needed to Apply Cover Letter & Resume Required MTSU offers a comprehensive benefits package, including but not limited to the following: Sick Leave Vacation Leave for Administrative/Classified Staff/12-month Faculty 13 paid University holidays Medical, dental, vision, and life insurance Retirement plans Optional 401K and 403B Deferred Compensation Plans Educational benefits for the employee and their spouse and dependents Click here for additional information. MTSU is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified individuals are encouraged to apply. Proof of U.S. citizenship or eligibility for U.S. employment is required before employment (Immigration Control Act of 1986). Clery Act crime statistics for MTSU are available at https://police.mtsu.edu/annual-security-report/ or by contacting MTSU Public Safety at (615) 898-2424. MTSU is a Tobacco & Drug-Free campus. This position requires a criminal background check. Therefore, you will be required to provide information about your criminal history to be considered. For individuals requiring reasonable accommodation to apply: In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation to apply for a position with MTSU, please call 615-898-2929 or email hrs@mtsu.edu. Application Review Date: September 22, 2026 Back to search results Apply Now First Name (required) 86b74965 Last Name (required) 221f71d1 Email (required) 47cd2fdf Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Specialist - Tech Support Murfreesboro, Tennessee, Tennessee Admissions and Enrollment, Information Technology Reporting to the Associate Director of Communications and Technology, maintains the data integrity and operations of the Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system (Slate), supporting the data and system functionality needed for communications and recruitment activities across Undergraduate Admissions and other Enrollment Management departments. Provide training and technical support to admissions staff in accessing and using Slate for various recruitment activities, promoting efficient and effective